rul:C-01 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "test coverage: abstract tests vs concrete applications" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:plan-walkthrough-2026-09-05 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:test-coverage ;
    ogc:problem "The paper draft conflates tests (abstract) that cover requirements with the concrete applications of those tests during a case, which produce the evidence. Z's comment on the draft (2026-09-05): \"it seems to conflate tests (abstract) with (concrete) applications of those tests ... test coverage ... relates the requirements we carry about to tests (abstract) that cover them; Not the specific incidents (plural) of those tests applied during a specific case. the latter produces the evidence which is ultimately rolled up to support validating (or invalidating) the hypothesis that the requirement is met.\" SEVOCAB carries ISO/IEC/IEEE 29119-2:2021 3.28 test coverage, which supports the abstract reading." ;
    ogc:severity "H" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "Z's comment on the paper draft; SEVOCAB entry check" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-02 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "operating environment: which canonical anchor" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:plan-walkthrough-2026-09-05 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:operational-environment ;
    ogc:problem "Term contract v5 anchors \"operating environment\" to the automotive Operational Design Domain (SAE J3016, SAE J3259, ISO 34503), all paid sources outside the evaluation domain. SEVOCAB carries \"operational environment\" (IEEE 982-2024 3.1): physical context, setting, and circumstances used to support the in-service operation of a system." ;
    ogc:severity "M" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "the authors' term contract draft review against SEVOCAB" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-03 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "operational envelope: no canonical entry" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:plan-walkthrough-2026-09-05 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:operational-envelope ;
    ogc:problem "Neither ISO 9000:2026 nor SEVOCAB defines \"operational envelope\". Term contract v5 cites process-safety usage (CCPS \"safe operating envelope\"), a weak fit. Functionally the envelope is the declared requirement set with its acceptance criteria and weights for the operational environment." ;
    ogc:severity "M" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "the authors' term contract draft review against ISO 9000:2026 and SEVOCAB" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-04 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "redistribution of source snapshots" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:plan-walkthrough-2026-09-05 ;
    ogc:problem "SEBoK v2.14 is CC BY-NC-SA; the ISO 9000:2026 OBP preview is copyrighted text captured as 37 screenshots. Committing either to a public repository is a licence exposure; not committing them weakens machine verification of quotes in CI." ;
    ogc:severity "M" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "source register design" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-05 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "deployment sensitivity: refined term or coinage" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:plan-walkthrough-2026-09-05 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:deployment-sensitivity ;
    ogc:problem "The weight on each acceptance criterion by consequence of failure. SEVOCAB carries risk-based testing (ISO/IEC/IEEE 29119-2:2021 3.16). Is \"deployment sensitivity\" a refinement of that or a fourth coinage." ;
    ogc:severity "L" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "coinage audit of the authors' term contract draft" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-06 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "IRI base: w3id now or Pages URL" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:plan-walkthrough-2026-09-05 ;
    ogc:problem "Ontology and record IRIs need a stable base. w3id.org/og-caie requires a PR to perma-id/w3id.org and resolves nowhere until merged; the GitHub Pages URL resolves immediately but renaming later breaks every Turtle file." ;
    ogc:severity "L" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "repository design" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-07 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "scope: requirements and interfaces, or architecture too" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:plan-walkthrough-2026-09-05 ;
    ogc:problem "Z's SEBoK screenshots draw the scope box around Concept Definition and System Requirements Definition (including Assess Interactions across Interfaces) and stop before Logical and Physical Architecture. The infra drawing (frontend, backend, data) is a realization sketch. Do part and port defs stay at the interface level or allocate to that drawing." ;
    ogc:severity "M" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "SEBoK v2.14 figures annotated by Z" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-08 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "adequacy vs appropriateness" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:plan-walkthrough-2026-09-05 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:appropriateness,
        term:sufficiency ;
    ogc:problem "The paper draft and the authors' term contract draft label the attestation's context judgment \"adequacy\". The primary source for the pairing (Hawkins, Kelly, Knight and Graydon 2011, assurance claim points) uses \"appropriateness\" for asserted context and \"sufficiency\" for asserted solution; ISA 500 uses appropriateness (quality) and sufficiency (quantity). \"Adequacy\" also collides with ISO 9000:2026 3.11.2 review." ;
    ogc:severity "H" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "Z's correction during planning; verified against Hawkins et al. 2011 sections 3.2 and 3.3 and ISA 500 paragraphs 5(b), 5(f), A8" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-09 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "the coinage set: which terms do we own" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:plan-walkthrough-2026-09-05 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:domain-specific-ontology,
        term:evaluation-process-ontology,
        term:og-caie ;
    ogc:problem "Term contract v5 tags probe/scenario, deployment sensitivity, DSO, EPO and CAIE as [CAIE] assemblies. Under the rule that terms are used, not owned, which of these are coinages the project must own, and which are refinements of standard terms." ;
    ogc:severity "H" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "coinage audit of the authors' term contract draft during planning" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-10 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "system under test: weak canonical entry" ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:test-item ;
    ogc:problem "SEVOCAB's only entry for \"system under test (SUT)\" reads \"parts of the CBSS to be tested\" (ISO/IEC 14756:1999, a performance-measurement standard). The cleaner entries are \"test item: work product to be tested\" (ISO/IEC/IEEE 29119-2:2021) and \"system-of-interest: system whose life cycle is under consideration\" (ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207:2026). The paper says \"system under test\" throughout. Options: keep SUT as prefLabel with the weak quote (current), or make \"test item\" canonical with SUT as altLabel." ;
    ogc:severity "L" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "SEVOCAB entry check while building the glossary" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-11 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "technical expert: one kind or several on the evaluation team" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:sheet-01-walkthrough-2026-09-06 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:technical-expert ;
    ogc:problem "ISO 9000:2026 3.12.9 defines technical expert in the audit context as a person who provides specific knowledge or expertise to the audit team. The glossary had bound it only to the DomainExpert part. Who else on the evaluation team is a technical expert, and in what." ;
    ogc:severity "M" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "row 6 of rulings sheet 01" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-12 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "assessing the assessors" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:sheet-01-walkthrough-2026-09-06 ;
    ogc:problem "Technical experts may in principle have mirrored counterparts who assess the assessment (second-party review, as in the June prototype's audit module). Does this specification model them." ;
    ogc:severity "L" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "row 6 of rulings sheet 01" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-13 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "the chain from requirement to attestation: is the test plan explicit" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:sheet-01-walkthrough-2026-09-06 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:acceptance-criteria,
        term:attestation,
        term:requirement ;
    ogc:problem "The record linked requirement to criterion, probe to criterion, run to probe, evidence to run, and attestation to criterion and evidence. It had no test plan node, no expected result on the criterion, and no binding from the attestation to the probe whose run produced its evidence, so the interpretation was not mechanically tied to the plan that produced what it interpreted." ;
    ogc:severity "H" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "row 7 of rulings sheet 01 (requirement), Z's question" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-14 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "probe versus run: trajectories, sessions and state feedback policies" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:sheet-01-walkthrough-2026-09-06 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:probe,
        term:test,
        term:test-plan ;
    ogc:problem "The record has one probe, one run and one evidence, which hides a distinction Z draws: a probe is an individual prompt-response pair; a run is a sequence of prompt-response pairs forming a trajectory within a session; sessions are stateful and LLM-system behaviour is highly context sensitive, nonlinear in the sense that a small change in input can cause large changes in output, especially when trajectories are continued. Test plans are not limited to single probes: they support strategies that determine probes according to a state feedback policy (semantic state feedback). Z: this is the place where a small amount of extra definition drawn from control engineering, system identification and metrology as applied to dynamical systems has the most to gain; hunt for canonical sources, starting with NIST." ;
    ogc:severity "H" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "row 8 of rulings sheet 01, Z's comment" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-15 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "operational envelope: what it adds to a set of requirements" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:sheet-01-walkthrough-2026-09-06 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:operational-envelope ;
    ogc:problem "R-03 kept operational envelope as a house label anchored to ISO 9000:2026 requirement. Is it merely the set of requirements, or does it carry more: the binding of those requirements to one system under test in one operational environment." ;
    ogc:severity "M" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "row 8 of rulings sheet 01" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-16 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "requirements traceability and metrological traceability" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:sheet-01-walkthrough-2026-09-06 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:requirements-traceability ;
    ogc:problem "ISO 9000:2026 3.5.11 Note 2 defers the metrological sense of traceability to ISO/IEC Guide 99 (the VIM). The glossary anchored requirements traceability to 29148 via SEVOCAB and kept metrology out. Should the metrological sense be visible, and how do the two relate." ;
    ogc:severity "M" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "row 9 of rulings sheet 01" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-17 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "conformity, conformance, and what SHACL calls validation" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:sheet-01-walkthrough-2026-09-06 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:conformance,
        term:conformity ;
    ogc:problem "ISO 9000:2026 3.5.9 deprecates conformance as a synonym of conformity. W3C SHACL calls its machine check validation, which by this specification's V and V split is verification. The glossary had one term, conformity, and banned conformance. How to name the machine-checked, correctly constructed record without confusing it with fulfilment of a requirement in the ISO sense, or with validation." ;
    ogc:severity "H" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "row 10 of rulings sheet 01" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-18 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "evaluation record: what the EPO binds it to provide" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:sheet-01-walkthrough-2026-09-06 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:evaluation-record ;
    ogc:problem "Is the evaluation record merely a record in the ISO sense, or is it bound by the EPO to contain what traceability and coverage need, and is that binding checkable." ;
    ogc:severity "M" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "row 13 of rulings sheet 01" ;
    ogc:surfacedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date .

rul:C-19 a ogc:Concern ;
    rdfs:label "evidence: at what level, and what it maps to" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy rul:sheet-01-walkthrough-2026-09-06 ;
    ogc:concernsTerm term:expected-results,
        term:objective-evidence ;
    ogc:problem "The record bound each evidence item to one turn's response and the attestation to the probe. Evidence can also exist at the session level (a trajectory) and rolled up over many sessions (a sensitivity test or robustness battery), so binding to a probe is too narrow; and nothing said what an evidence item is evidence of." ;
    ogc:severity "H" ;
    ogc:status "ruled" ;
    ogc:surfacedHow "row 14 of rulings sheet 01" ;
