rul:R-07 a ogc:Ruling ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo rul:Z ;
    ogc:changeNote "SysML carries part, port, interface, action and requirement defs only; no allocation, no physical structure; the infra drawing is cited as a realization sketch." ;
    ogc:order 7 ;
    ogc:resolves rul:C-07 ;
    ogc:rulingText "The scope is requirements and interfaces; architecture is excluded. Part and port definitions stay at the interface level, and the infrastructure drawing is cited as a realization sketch with nothing allocated to it." ;
    ogc:verbatim "Yes: requirements + interfaces, no architecture" .

rul:R-14 a ogc:Ruling ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo rul:Z ;
    ogc:changeNote "Anchor unchanged (ISO 9000:2026 3.5.1 requirement, specializes). Narrative and scope note rewritten. EPO: RequirementSet names its system under test (epo:systemUnderTest, an earl:TestSubject) as well as its environment; shape S2 requires both; SysML RequirementSet gains sutNamed and SCI-02 checks it; the measles record names chatbot v1." ;
    ogc:order 14 ;
    ogc:resolves rul:C-15 ;
    ogc:rulingText "The operational envelope refines the concept of requirements in its specificity: it conditions explicitly on an operating environment and on the system under test, stating that this system in this environment must meet these requirements. It is closely related to a set of requirements, but Contextual AI Evaluation expects different requirements for different systems under test in different operating environments. The distinction is deliberate: it separates the method from benchmarks and aligns it with the practice for safety-critical systems." ;
    ogc:verbatim "operational envelope refines the the concept of requirements in its specificity. an operational envelope explicit conditions on an operating environment and the system under test. we are saying THIS system in the THIS environment must meet THESE requirements. its closely related to set of requirements but we're really leaning into the Contextual AI Evaluation so we expect different requirements for different systems under test in different operating environments. this is explicitly to make this distinct from benchmarks are more like safety critical systems" .

