rul:R-09 a ogc:Ruling ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo rul:Z ;
    ogc:changeNote "Coinage is exactly three: Domain-Specific Ontology, Evaluation Process Ontology, OG-CAIE (the method name). Probe and deployment sensitivity are refined terms (R-05); operational envelope is a house label (R-03). Julie Hollek and Z agreed the DSO and EPO expansions in the paper comments (a co-author's note, 2026-09-05)." ;
    ogc:order 9 ;
    ogc:resolves rul:C-09 ;
    ogc:rulingText "Coinage is confined to the project's novel contributions. The two primary coinages are Domain-Specific Ontology and Evaluation Process Ontology; the method is named either CAIE or Ontology-Grounded CAIE, abbreviated OG-CAIE." ;
    ogc:verbatim "we have two primary coinages \"Domain-Specific Ontology\" and \"Evaluation Process Ontology\" ... focusing coinage only where it directly relates to our novel contributions ... feels like we would either stick with \"CAIE\" or Ontology-Grounded CAIE, which would OG-CAIE" .

rul:R-12 a ogc:Ruling ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo rul:Z ;
    ogc:changeNote "Added, never overwriting: glossary terms test plan and expected results (SEVOCAB, 29119); seeAlso test execution on test, test result on attestation, test scenario (29119-11) on scenario. EPO: TestPlan (objectives, means), expectedResult on the criterion, underPlan from attestation to probe. Record: the plan, expected results on a1-a3, both attestations bound to probe-1, recommendation derived from the plan. Shapes: S2 criterion requires an expected result; S3-TestPlan; S3 probe must be a plan's means; S6 chain rule (evidence used comes from a run of the bound probe which exercises the attested criterion); S8 recommendation names the plan. Counterexample attestation-off-plan. Model: TestPlan item, expectedResultStated, probeId on the attestation, SCI-04 and SCI-06 extended. Traceback query returns plan, probe and expected result." ;
    ogc:order 12 ;
    ogc:resolves rul:C-13 ;
    ogc:rulingText "Traceability from the requirement, as a hypothesis that may be falsified, through an epistemically valid process that collects and interprets evidence to render the judgement, is critical for requirements to be useful concepts. The existing definitions are not to be overwritten. The record must carry a chain of evidence connecting the test plans to the evidence they would produce, the implementation of those plans that produces the evidence, the interpretation of that evidence, and the justified attestation that a requirement is or is not met, bound to that evidence and to the test plan that produced it. This is the level of abstraction at which the abstract EPO is encoded." ;
    ogc:verbatim "in my experience the traceability from the requirement (as hypothesis that may be falsified) and the epistemically valid process that collects and interprets evidence to render the judgement is critical for requirements to be useful concepts. i do not want you to overwrite the definitions i want you to ensure we have a chain of evidence connecting test plans to the evidence they would produce to the implementation of those plans to that produces evidence to the interpretation of that evidence to make a justified attestation that a requirement is or is not met bound to that evidence and the test plan that produced it. this is the level of abstraction at which we are encoding our abstract EPO." .

rul:R-23 a ogc:Ruling ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo rul:Z ;
    ogc:changeNote "Three abstract actor categories, each a distinct part def and EPO slot, all held by the testing organization (accountExecutive[1]; team.domainExpert[1..*]; team.operator[1..*]; shape M5-Cardinality): DomainExpert, EvaluationOperator (headword evaluation operator, refined from the SEVOCAB operator; AI evaluation expert becomes its altLabel) and AccountExecutive (signatory and legal representative of the testing organization; no evidence, determination or attestation port). The worked example names Mala (account executive), Annie (domain expert) and Theo (evaluation operator); the record and the record page state that the case is synthetic, that the names recognise the roles of real people, and that no attestation in the record was made by them." ;
    ogc:order 23 ;
    ogc:resolves rul:C-23 ;
    ogc:rulingText """A domain expert and an evaluation operator are abstract actor categories that populate distinct slots in the EPO. There is also an account executive on the side of the evaluation organization, who is the signatory on the contract and the legal representative of the organization performing the evaluation.

The worked example names the Humane Intelligence executive (Mala), the domain expert (Annie) and the evaluation operator (Theo). These are references to real people, but the case is synthetic: the people named will recognise their roles, and they are not asked to make attestations within the demonstration case, which is a simplified synthetic walkthrough of the process.

DomainExpert, EvaluationOperator and AccountExecutive are all roles held by members of the company performing the evaluation. Each role must be filled, so there is an at-least-one rule. The account executive is exactly one, being the counterparty who represents the organization in the contract; the domain expert and evaluation operator roles are one or more.""" ;
    ogc:verbatim """you need a domain expert and an evaluation operator they are abstract actor categories that populate distinct slots in the EPO. there is also an account executive on the side of the evaluation org who is the signatory on the contract and the legal representative of the org performing the eval. 

our worked example names the HI executive (Mala), the Domain Expert Annie and the eval operator Theo. this are references to real people but the case is synthetic. the real people will read this and appreciate having their roles recognized but are not being asked to make attestations within the demo case which is a simplified synthetic walkthrough of the process / just to clarify "DomainExpert, EvaluationOperator and AccountExecutive" are all members of the company performing the eval. these are roles. the accountexec is limited to cardinality 1 but we allow more domain experts and operators to be on the team. / each role must be filled so there is an at least one rule. this means exec is exactly one since they are the counterparty representing the org in the contract. the the domain expert and eval operator roles are one or more""" .

term:deployment-sensitivity a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "risk weight"@en,
        "weight"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch src:sevocab_risk-based-testing ;
    skos:definition "The weight each acceptance criterion carries, set by the consequence of the system getting it wrong in this deployment. Coverage is computed against these weights so it reflects consequence rather than count."@en ;
    skos:inScheme ogc:Glossary ;
    skos:prefLabel "deployment sensitivity"@en ;
    skos:related term:risk-based-testing,
        term:test-coverage ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom rul:R-05 ;
    ogc:anchorRelation "specializes" ;
    ogc:binding "epo:weight; sysml attribute weight on AcceptanceCriterion" ;
    ogc:canonical [ ogc:cites src:sevocab ;
            ogc:locator "risk-based testing, p. 362 (fragment of the entry)" ;
            ogc:pdfPage 362 ;
            ogc:quote "prioritization, and use of testing activities and resources are consciously based on corresponding types and levels of analyzed risk" ;
            ogc:quoteStatus "machine" ] ;
    ogc:class "refined" .

term:guardrail a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader term:requirement ;
    skos:definition "A requirement on the system stating what may be shared with a user and what must be withheld. Recommendations at the end of an evaluation typically propose changes to guardrails."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch src:nist-ai-700-2_guardrail ;
    skos:inScheme ogc:Glossary ;
    skos:prefLabel "guardrail"@en ;
    skos:related term:red-teaming ;
    ogc:binding "epo:Recommendation targets a guardrail" ;
    ogc:canonical [ ogc:cites src:nist-ai-700-2 ;
            ogc:locator "Appendix A, Guardrail, p. 17 (first sentence of the entry)" ;
            ogc:pdfPage 24 ;
            ogc:quote "An application requirement specifying both 1) permitted information that can be shared with a user, and 2) prohibited information that should be withheld from a user." ;
            ogc:quoteStatus "machine" ] ;
    ogc:class "adopted" .

term:performance a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A measurable result. Here: how the system did on what was exercised, reported as the pass, fail and cannot-tell fractions of the covered criteria. Never merged with coverage."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch src:iso-9000-2026_3.7.3 ;
    skos:inScheme ogc:Glossary ;
    skos:prefLabel "performance"@en ;
    skos:related term:measurement-uncertainty,
        term:test-coverage ;
    ogc:binding "epo:Report passRate, failRate, cantTellRate" ;
    ogc:canonical [ ogc:cites src:iso-9000-2026 ;
            ogc:file "sources/local/iso-9000-2026/iso-9000-2026-obp-17.png" ;
            ogc:locator "3.7.3" ;
            ogc:quote "measurable result" ;
            ogc:quoteStatus "human" ;
            ogc:verifiedBy rul:Z ;
            ogc:verifiedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ] ;
    ogc:class "adopted" .

term:red-teaming a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A testing level in which human testers probe the system adversarially to see whether it stays within its guardrails. One way to run the probes in step four."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch src:nist-ai-700-2_red-teaming ;
    skos:inScheme ogc:Glossary ;
    skos:prefLabel "red teaming"@en ;
    skos:related term:evaluation-operator,
        term:guardrail,
        term:test-strategy ;
    ogc:binding "sysml part def EvaluationOperator (red teamer); epo:Session with a prov:Person in the evaluation operator role" ;
    ogc:canonical [ ogc:cites src:nist-ai-700-2 ;
            ogc:locator "Appendix A, Red teaming, p. 17" ;
            ogc:pdfPage 24 ;
            ogc:quote "Testing level which evaluates whether applications adhere to guardrails in response to adversarial prompting or stress testing by human testers." ;
            ogc:quoteStatus "machine" ] ;
    ogc:class "adopted" .

term:second-party-conformity-assessment-activity a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "second party"@en ;
    skos:definition "Evaluation performed by, or on behalf of, an organization with a user interest in the test item: a purchaser, a regulator, a deploying agency. A sponsor that is not the test item provider commissions the evaluation in this position."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch src:iso-iec-17000-2020_4.4 ;
    skos:inScheme ogc:Glossary ;
    skos:prefLabel "second-party conformity assessment activity"@en ;
    skos:related term:evaluation-customer,
        term:first-party-conformity-assessment-activity,
        term:third-party-conformity-assessment-activity ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom rul:R-21 ;
    ogc:binding "epo:sponsorRole when the sponsor is not the test item provider (record fact epo:isAccountable, S0)" ;
    ogc:canonical [ ogc:cites src:iso-iec-17000-2020 ;
            ogc:locator "4.4 second-party conformity assessment activity" ;
            ogc:quote "conformity assessment activity that is performed by a person or organization that has a user interest in the object of conformity assessment" ;
            ogc:quoteStatus "human" ;
            ogc:verifiedBy rul:Z ;
            ogc:verifiedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ] ;
    ogc:class "adopted" .

term:test-case a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Inputs, execution conditions and expected results developed for a particular objective. The abstract test; a probe is a test case tied to the criteria it exercises."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch src:sevocab_test-case ;
    skos:inScheme ogc:Glossary ;
    skos:narrower term:probe ;
    skos:prefLabel "test case"@en ;
    skos:related term:expected-results,
        term:scenario ;
    ogc:binding "epo:Probe" ;
    ogc:canonical [ ogc:cites src:sevocab ;
            ogc:locator "test case, p. 432" ;
            ogc:pdfPage 432 ;
            ogc:quote "set of test inputs, execution conditions, and expected results developed for a particular objective, such as to exercise a particular program path or to verify compliance with a specific requirement" ;
            ogc:quoteStatus "machine" ] ;
    ogc:class "adopted" .

term:test-suite a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "battery"@en,
        "robustness battery"@en ;
    skos:definition "A set of sessions run together, for example replicate sessions of one strategy, or the varied sessions of a sensitivity test or robustness battery. Evidence rolled up over a suite is evidence at the third level, above probe and session."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch src:sevocab_test-suite ;
    skos:inScheme ogc:Glossary ;
    skos:prefLabel "test suite"@en ;
    skos:related term:repeatability,
        term:session ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom rul:R-18 ;
    ogc:binding "epo:TestSuite, a prov:Activity grouping epo:Session activities" ;
    ogc:canonical [ ogc:cites src:sevocab ;
            ogc:locator "test suite, p. 439" ;
            ogc:pdfPage 439 ;
            ogc:quote "set of test cases or test procedures" ;
            ogc:quoteStatus "machine" ] ;
    ogc:class "adopted" ;
    ogc:seeAlso [ ogc:cites src:sevocab ;
            ogc:locator "robustness, p. 363 (ISO/IEC 25059:2023)" ;
            ogc:pdfPage 363 ;
            ogc:quote "degree to which an AI system can maintain its level of functional correctness under any circumstances" ;
            ogc:quoteStatus "machine" ] .

term:third-party-conformity-assessment-activity a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "independent testing"@en,
        "third party"@en ;
    skos:definition "Evaluation performed by an organization independent of the provider of the test item and with no user interest in it, and not on behalf of anyone who has one. Independence of the testing organization from the test item provider is what makes an OG-CAIE result independent; the record states it as a fact about the parties rather than assuming it, and states separately whether the sponsor has a user interest."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch src:iso-iec-17000-2020_4.5 ;
    skos:inScheme ogc:Glossary ;
    skos:prefLabel "third-party conformity assessment activity"@en ;
    skos:related term:evaluation-service-provider,
        term:first-party-conformity-assessment-activity,
        term:second-party-conformity-assessment-activity ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom rul:R-21 ;
    ogc:binding "epo:independentOfAccountable on the testing organization (record fact, S0)" ;
    ogc:canonical [ ogc:cites src:iso-iec-17000-2020 ;
            ogc:locator "4.5 third-party conformity assessment activity" ;
            ogc:quote "conformity assessment activity that is performed by a person or organization that is independent of the provider of the object of conformity assessment and has no user interest in the object" ;
            ogc:quoteStatus "human" ;
            ogc:verifiedBy rul:Z ;
            ogc:verifiedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ] ;
    ogc:class "adopted" .

term:validation a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Confirming with objective evidence that the requirements for a specific intended use were fulfilled. Applied to the evaluation itself: was it aimed at the right problem and is the evidence enough. Both are human judgments, recorded in the attestation."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch src:iso-9000-2026_3.11.14 ;
    skos:inScheme ogc:Glossary ;
    skos:prefLabel "validation"@en ;
    skos:related term:appropriateness,
        term:attestation,
        term:verification ;
    ogc:binding "epo:Attestation (human); SCI requirements tagged human" ;
    ogc:canonical [ ogc:cites src:iso-9000-2026 ;
            ogc:file "sources/local/iso-9000-2026/iso-9000-2026-obp-32.png" ;
            ogc:locator "3.11.14" ;
            ogc:quote "confirmation, through the provision of objective evidence, that the requirements for a specific intended use or application have been fulfilled" ;
            ogc:quoteStatus "human" ;
            ogc:verifiedBy rul:Z ;
            ogc:verifiedOn "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ] ;
    ogc:class "adopted" ;
    ogc:seeAlso [ ogc:cites src:sevocab ;
            ogc:locator "validation, p. 464" ;
            ogc:pdfPage 464 ;
            ogc:quote "confirmation, through the provision of objective evidence, that the requirements for a specific intended use or application have been fulfilled" ;
            ogc:quoteStatus "machine" ] .

